cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Primordia in research or teaching, please cite it as below."
title: "Primordia: a GPU artificial-life laboratory"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "The Primordia contributors"
    alias: skulitom
abstract: >-
  Primordia is a GPU artificial-life laboratory written in Rust with wgpu. It runs five real-time simulations on
  compute shaders: Physarum slime mould, Particle Life, Lenia, Gray-Scott reaction-diffusion and Symbiosis, which
  couples agents with chemistry. It measures every world live on the GPU, renders stills, videos and galleries
  headlessly, and searches each world's parameters for novel behaviour.
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-09-20"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/skulitom/primordia"
keywords:
  - artificial life
  - emergence
  - physarum
  - particle life
  - lenia
  - reaction-diffusion
  - cellular automata
  - agent-based model
  - novelty search
  - gpu
  - wgpu
